nd even during  the throes of this hurricane including a  tweet bragging about pardoning racist  Arizona sheriff Joe Arpaio who was  convicted of committing human rights  abuses will talk in more detail about  that pardoned later but Donald Trump  again when you've got a huge portion of  the country preparing for what was at  that point clearly going to be a  devastating storm he goes to Twitter and  he says I'm pleased to inform you that I  have just granted a full pardon  capitalising pardon why we don't know  - 85 year-old American patriot Sheriff  Joe Arpaio he kept America Arizona safe  Trump also choosing Friday night as the  right time to announce his new directive  to the Defense Department to conduct a  study on transgender people in the  military another issue that's been part  of the totally pointless gong show of  so-called governance under Donald Trump  and at first I thought oh it's  insensitive timing talking about our  piyo and the Department of Defense  transgender thing and then I realize no  this was probably deliberate the White  House choosing to talk about these  issues at this time so that it would  hopefully be buried by news about  hurricane Harvey and then Donald Trump  spent the rest of the weekend continuing  to show Americans just how focused he  was on hurricane Harvey Sunday morning  in the midst of the disaster in Texas  Trump posts a tweet promoting his  friend's new book this was written by  Milwaukee's controversial Sheriff David  Clarke who's called Planned Parenthood  genocidal and is called black people  lazy and morally corrupt Donald Trump  goes to Twitter and says a great book by  a great guy highly recommended and you  see there it is a link to David Clarke  Jr's book a horrible book by the way  people are telling me and reading  reading very very important I'm one of  the best people at reading but people  say trust me folks one of the best books  an hour and a half later he gets back on  Twitter and starts bragging about how he  won the state of Missouri during the  election and  criticize Connecticut Senator Chris  Murphy for opposing his tax cuts  tweeting again floodwaters continuing to  rise Trump goes to Twitter I will also  be going to a wonderful state Missouri  that I won by a lot in 2016 16 Democrats  cm meaning Chris Murphy is opposed to  big big tax cuts Republican will win s  Murphy responded by tweeting my god at  this exact moment people are dying in  the worst natural disaster of his  presidency and instead of leading he's  attacking Democrats and then 30 minutes  later Donald Trump starts tweeting about  how Mexico is going to pay for the wall  bringing that nonsense back to life  tweeting with Mexico being one of the  highest crime nations in the world we  must have the wall Mexico will pay for  it through reimbursement slash other why  do I feel that reimbursement slash other  is a category that plays into the  potential tax fraud that Donald Trump  has committed maybe will someday find  out about that and of course at this  point multiple people had been confirmed  dead by the hurricane Trump still had  not mentioned their deaths five minutes  later he starts complaining about trade  negotiations with Mexico and Canada  quote we are in the NAFTA worst trade  deal ever made renegotiation process  with Mexico and Canada both being very  difficult may have to terminate the  tweets Donald Trump did ultimately send  about the hurricane are mostly patting  himself on the back talking about the  great response that the White House  coordinated whatever and here's the sick  irony or the sick reality of it  President Obama passed a regulation in  2015 to make our infrastructure more  flood proof remember infrastructure was  going to be a big part of trumps  administration two weeks ago Trump  reversed that regulation before it even  took effect it would have required new  bridges roads other structures to be  built on safer ground that's susceptible  to flooding during hurr